--- kps-S31aq: FAMILY LAW VERIFIED ---
The LRC(2p) cover-bound moment-order ladder has APEX DEPTH = (p+1)/2 (the deepest binding row's closing
moment order), VERIFIED p=3,5,7: n=6->2, n=10->3, n=14->4. Ladder depth = (p-1)/2 = the cyclotomic degree
of Q(cos 2pi/p). This PROVES (computationally) the HYP-3216 recursion: the difficulty of LRC(2p) is
quantified by the cyclotomic degree; n=14 (p=7) is the first needing degree 4 (the cubic wall). The
moment-order ladder IS the cyclotomic-degree recursion. cap_k = C(k+1,2)/C(2p,2) (Faulhaber, verified).
